{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 proof that Zhi-Wei Sun's conjecture (ii) for OEIS A234360 is false, in the form stated by Formal Conjectures: for n = 1408 there is no 0 < k < n and prime p with (p + k)^2 = (k + 1)^φ(n − k). Equivalently, none of the numbers (k + 1)^(φ(1408 − k)/2) − k is prime. Each of the 1407 cases is closed by a kernel-checked certificate: a small prime factor (1281 cases), a failed Fermat test to base 2 (121 cases, numbers of 466 to 1392 digits), or a trivial size argument (5 cases).",
